  "verbalization": "Cephalexin, a member of the cephalosporin class, is linked to Slc22a6 through a series of hierarchical and structural relationships. The evidence suggests that Cephalexin, as part of the broader cephalosporin family, binds to Slc22a6 through a common pathway involving cephalosporin antibiotics. This connection is reinforced by the fact that multiple cephalosporins, including Cefazolin and Ceftriaxone, share a common ancestor with Cephalexin and all bind to Slc22a6. The recurring mechanism involves the interaction of cephalosporin antibiotics with Slc22a6, which is a transporter involved in drug efflux and ion transport. The integration of these paths highlights a potential role for Slc22a6 in the pharmacological action of cephalosporins, though the exact mechanism of binding remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a general relationship between cephalosporin antibiotics and Slc22a6, emphasizing the importance of transporter interactions in drug action.",
